# Accessibility

This project uses the [a11y-skills](https://github.com/Elizabeth1979/a11y-skills) pattern library.

**Route before you read.** Open `patterns/INDEX.md` — it maps a UI element or an audit symptom to
exactly one pattern file — then read only that file. The 40 pattern files are 8–16 KB each;
loading them all wastes context.

**Non-negotiable defaults**

- Native HTML before ARIA + JavaScript. An ARIA role is a promise to implement its whole keyboard model.
- No redundant ARIA (`<button role="button">` is noise).
- Keyboard-operable, sensible tab order, visible focus indicator on every interactive element.
- An accessible name on every control.
- Dynamic changes announced via live region or a deliberate focus move.

**Scope.** Retrofitting an existing page changes markup and ARIA only — no restyling. The
exceptions are colour contrast and reduced motion, which are inherently visual; fix those in CSS
and say so.

**Verify.** Run `docs/verification.md`, then report which criteria still need a human pass.
